  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Sunday)\nIssued at 1241 PM CDT MON SEP 28 2026\n\nWater vapor imagery this morning reveals an upper trough cutting\nacross the Tennessee Valley and an upper level ridge out to our\nwest. If we look closely, we can see a shortwave rotating along\nthe western periphery of the trough. This feature will move\nthrough the area over the next couple of days. However, the lack\nof sufficient moisture will keep us dry for the next several\ndays. Similar to yesterday, the KBMX radar is picking up some\nlight shower activity. It is very unlikely that any of this\nprecipitation will make it to the surface as we have much drier\nair in the low levels per the 12Z KBMX sounding.\n\nLow to medium chances for showers and storms return to the\nforecast late in the week as a stout upper trough moves across\nthe Plains. An associated cold front will head our way late in\nthe work week, eventually working through the region over the\nweekend. The exact timing remains uncertain at this time as there\nare some signs of it stalling over the first half of the weekend\nbefore pushing through. Regardless, we are looking at low to\nmedium chances for showers and storms returning to the forecast\nFriday afternoon and continuing into early next week as southerly\nflow ushers a healthy plume of tropical moisture across the\nsoutheast. Forecast soundings hint at a skinny CAPE profile and a\nwarm cloud depth up to 15kft, suggesting locally heavy rainfall\nis likely with any shower or storm over the weekend. Rainfall\namounts are likely to range from 2-3\" Friday through the weekend\nwith a low (15-20%) chance for amounts of 3\" per the latest LREF.\n\nWe kick off a warming trend this week with highs rebounding into\nthe low 90s by Wednesday. Drier air in place will help us\nmaintain our cooler mornings with lows dropping down into the mid\n50s to around 60 degrees through mid week. As we head into the\nlate stages of the work week, a moist southerly flow will bump\nout overnight lows up into the upper 60s to low 70s. Increased\nrain chances/cloud cover will help knock a few degrees off our\nhighs next weekend.\n\n95/Castillo",
